// window/x11/bind/xcursor.cst — Xcursor: the pointer the user chose.
//
// The core protocol's cursors are the 77 shapes in cursorfont.h, drawn as 1-bit
// masks at whatever size 1987 thought was right. Every modern desktop replaces
// them with a theme — a named set of ARGB images, possibly animated, at a size
// the user picked — and Xcursor is how a client honours that.
//
// ../cursor.cst uses XcursorLibraryLoadCursor, which resolves a shape name
// through the user's configured theme and falls back to the core font when
// there is no theme. A program that does not link this still gets a cursor; it
// just gets the 1987 one.
//
// XcursorImageCreate and XcursorImageLoadCursor are the other half: a cursor
// built from pixels the program drew, which is what a custom crosshair or a
// drag-and-drop image is.

